      "id": 1,
      "text": "Manchester was founded on land acquired by John Nickey in 1740, an heir of William Penn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://manchesterborough.gov/about/history-of-the-borough/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1814, William Reeser bought the town’s land, noting its proximity to the Susquehanna River and southern markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://manchesterborough.gov/about/history-of-the-borough/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s streets look like they did 150 years ago, except for modern development and traffic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
